  "student_passage": "Last Tuesday, our class made a map of the school yard. Ms Reed gave us (1) ____ large sheet of paper and asked us to mark the paths. We worked in pairs. My partner, June, carried a ruler, and I brought two (2) ____.\n\nWe started beside the gate. June (3) ____ the distance to the first tree while I wrote it down. It was longer (4) ____ we had expected. We could not measure it with one short ruler, (5) ____ we used a long string instead.\n\nBefore we drew the lines, Ms Reed asked, “Whose notes are these?” “They are (6) ____,” we answered. She reminded us to put both our names on the page. Then she showed us how (7) ____ the lengths smaller for the map.\n\nBy the end of the lesson, every pair had a map. June pointed to ours and said, “Look! The path by the wall is the (8) ____ one.” It was shorter than all the other paths we had measured. Tomorrow we (9) ____ the maps with another class. If we find a mistake, we (10) ____ it before putting our work on the wall.",
